                'The rows of Vᵀ are the principal directions, ordered from most to least spread. The first points along the long axis of the cloud.',
                'The singular values in Σ say how much spread each direction has: the variance along direction k is σₖ² / (n − 1).',
                'The share of variance explained by direction k is σₖ² / Σσ². If the first two directions explain 95%, two numbers per sample keep almost everything.',
                'Project onto the top k directions: Z = X·Vₖ. Each sample is now k numbers instead of d.',
                'To go back approximately, compute Z·Vₖᵀ and add the mean. What is lost is exactly the spread along the dropped directions.',
